    {
      "id": "7a1e0b52-3c4d-4e5f-8a01-000000000001",
      "name": "Setup notes",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -740,
        -610
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 900,
        "height": 440,
        "content": "## PSL X publisher - SCHEDULED + MANUAL\n**Imports inactive. This can publish real approved posts after activation.**\n\nAlready configured: every hour at :00 and :30; America/Phoenix; https://www.psllabs.org. Manual and scheduled runs are labelled separately.\n\n**Select existing credentials on 8 HTTP nodes:**\n- **PSL X Queue** (Header Auth): Claim work; Report account check; Request dispatch permit; Report create result; Report lookup evidence.\n- **PSL X Publishing** (generic OAuth2): Get authenticated X account; Create Post on X; Look up post on X.\n\n**Start safely:** Pause new dispatches at /admin-social; keep the old workflow unpublished; import into a NEW workflow; attach the credentials; publish THIS workflow only. Check the first automatic execution with nothing due. Then approve a future dated post and resume the queue.\n\nKeep one scheduled publisher. Do not replay old executions, pin response data, or run Create Post by itself. No automatic create retry. Outcome unknown means review, never repost blindly. Existing approval/account/daily-cap checks remain on PSL. The timer checks the queue; it does not invent or approve content.\n48 timer executions/day (about 1,440 per 30 days), plus manual/other workflows.\n35 nodes; 8 HTTP nodes. No credentials or credential IDs are included."
      }
    },
